(1) Codimension / transverse phase space (theorem half):
  Vortex worldsheet is 1+1 dimensional; transverse space is R^{d_⊥}.
  Loop production = reconnection of two segments approaching in the
  transverse plane. The integer count of independent transverse
  directions is d_⊥ = 2.
  Solid-angle ratio Ω(S^{d_⊥−1}) / Ω(S^{d−1}) = 2π/4π = 1/2 is a
  *reduction* of bare 3D direction measure — it does NOT by itself
  produce an enhancement factor 2. The factor 2 is the *dimension*
  of the transverse plane, not a solid-angle ratio.

(2) Microscopic → VOS map:
  ρ̇|_chop = − c_chop μ v / ξ³     (VOS definition)
  ṅ_int   ~ v / ξ⁴                (one-scale meetings)
  energy removed per loop-forming reconnection ~ μ α ξ
  ⇒ c_chop = C_geom · p · α · f_ℓ

  Forced on the overdamped PRTOE branch:
    p   = 1   continuum superfluid vortices always reconnect
    α   = 1   one-scale: only length is ξ (no α≪1 cascade)
    f_ℓ = 1   one-scale self-similarity (order-unity loop fraction)
  ⇒ c_chop = C_geom

