(4) Why primary is T (c_chop = d_⊥), not S or A:
  • VOS already feeds the RMS segment speed v into ξ̇ = ½ c v.
    Orientation is inside that average. Multiplying by ⟨|sin θ|⟩
    again double-counts angles → reject S as the full answer.
  • A = d_⊥·⟨|sin θ|⟩ reintroduces the same double-count on top of
    the DOF factor; keep as a sensitivity check only.
  • T = d_⊥ counts independent transverse approach channels once,
    matches the unique integer geometric invariant of the embedding,
    and is the non-double-counting closure.
  • L = 1 is the coefficient-free floor (Route L); right scale,
    missing the transverse channel count.

